<div data-wf-id="b4b06fdc-c36e-681c-353a-414d5e3096c8" data-w-id="b4b06fdc-c36e-681c-353a-414d5e3096c8" class="why-process-card">
UR &amp; RCM
</div>
<div slot="content-2" data-wf-id="15b1c087-215a-56d2-dcde-db913ad3f1d5" data-w-id="15b1c087-215a-56d2-dcde-db913ad3f1d5" class="why-process-card">
Documentation
</div>
<div slot="content-3" data-wf-id="54930475-252d-bf88-664c-80d180f8d972" data-w-id="54930475-252d-bf88-664c-80d180f8d972" class="why-process-card">
Session
</div>
</ElementProcessGrid>
<UtilitySpacer size="large" />
<p data-wf-id="e6b9a55d-0185-cd00-2b5a-0ea83bf2f6d3" data-w-id="e6b9a55d-0185-cd00-2b5a-0ea83bf2f6d3" class="text-align-center text-size-large margin-0auto max-width-large">
Every RCM tool only ever sees the claim. Every compliance tool only ever sees the chart. Soulside runs on the same record as your documentation and your UR: the actual session. Not a summary handed off from another system.
</p>
<ElementContentGroup contentTextWrap="balance" bodyRichTextFontSize="medium" bodyRichTextTag="p" headingVisibility={false} taglineVisibility={false} contentMaxWidth="xlarge" contentAlignment="center">
<GlobalDemoButton />
<Fragment slot="bodyrichtext">So when a claim fails, Soulside does not just flag it. It traces the failure back to the session or template that caused it, because it is the only platform that was there for both the care and the claim.</Fragment>
</ElementContentGroup>
<ElementContentGroup slot="content-first" contentTextWrap="balance" buttonGroupVisibility={false} bodyRichTextFontSize="medium" bodyRichTextTag="p" bodyVisibility={false} contentMaxWidth="xlarge" contentAlignment="center">
<Fragment slot="bodyrichtext">Documentation deficiencies don't just create audit exposure. They create denial risk, authorization gaps, and clawback liability. Soulside catches these before any of that happens.</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="headingtext">One evidence chain. From session to reimbursement.</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="taglinetext">Why Soulside</Fragment>
</ElementContentGroup>
</Layout2>
</Section>
<Section sectionColorScheme="lightest" sectionContainer="large">
<Layout2 layout="stack">
<LayoutGridSlot gridSlotColumnsMobileL={1} gridSlotColumnsTablet={2} gridSlotColumnsDesktop={2}>
<ElementCard buttonVisibility={false} bodyRichTextTag="p" headingStyle="h4" taglineVisibility={false} visualVisibility={true}>
<ElementTagline variant="white">
Revenue Cycle Leadership
</ElementTagline>
<UtilitySpacer size="medium-flex-grow" />
<Fragment slot="bodyrichtext">Speed changes which pile a claim lands in. Every hour off the documentation lockout is an hour your appeal team gets back before the window closes.</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="headingtext">The leak is not your overturn rate. It is the appeals you never file.</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="taglinetext">Revenue Cycle Leadership</Fragment>
</ElementCard>
<ElementCard buttonVisibility={false} bodyRichTextTag="p" headingStyle="h4" taglineVisibility={false} visualVisibility={true}>
<ElementTagline variant="white">
Executive Leadership and CFOs
</ElementTagline>
<UtilitySpacer size="medium-flex-grow" />
<Fragment slot="bodyrichtext">When medical necessity cannot be justified in time, patients stay uncovered on your dime. Soulside proves it before submission, not after the denial.</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="headingtext">Every uncovered day hits your bottom line.</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="taglinetext">Executive Leadership and CFOs</Fragment>
</ElementCard>
<ElementCard buttonVisibility={false} bodyRichTextTag="p" headingStyle="h4" taglineVisibility={false} visualVisibility={true}>
<ElementTagline variant="white">
Clinical Directors and Managers
</ElementTagline>
<UtilitySpacer size="medium" />
<Fragment slot="bodyrichtext">Checking off a signature does not prove medical necessity to an auditor. Soulside scans every note for clinical logic and session accuracy, so clinicians focus on care.</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="headingtext">A safety net, not a checklist.</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="taglinetext">Clinical Directors and Managers</Fragment>
</ElementCard>
<ElementCard buttonVisibility={false} bodyRichTextTag="p" headingStyle="h4" taglineVisibility={false} visualVisibility={true}>
<ElementTagline variant="white">
Compliance and Legal
</ElementTagline>
<UtilitySpacer size="medium-flex-grow" />
<Fragment slot="bodyrichtext">Every note is still clinician-reviewed and signed. Soulside compresses the time to a compliant signature, it does not change who signs or what is required. Contemporaneous documentation is also easier to defend in an audit than notes reconstructed under time pressure.</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="headingtext">Faster signatures, same signer.</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="taglinetext">Compliance and Legal</Fragment>
</ElementCard>
